 in a new log entry): THE LOG'S ENTRY FOR THE FIRST THREE PARTS OF THE SERIES,
 WITH THE TWO CORRECTIONS THE ROWS ASK FOR.

One entry at the head of the changelog and its pair at the end of the progress log, written by the building session for main to reword at the landing. They say what the three parts mend, that no statement of the mathematics is the builder's, and what is not done. THEY CARRY: the correction of the changelog's sentence of 2026-11-11 on the index of a unit on one line (the SM seat's 27), in main's words from the law map; and a line on main's own use of the word "reproduced" on 2026-11-12 (the SM seat's 5).

B1894's test of the old sign counts the old words on the changelog twice with this patch: once in the entry of 2026-11-11, once in the entry that corrects them, with the sign beside them. The front page's state block and the page of context are made again.

ON THE COUNT OF LANDINGS: on this seat's chain, where each patch is a commit, the count since the review's anchor passes 40 within this part, and the gate on it says that the review fires. It is so from this part's eleventh patch on main's line, which has one commit more. It is a count and not a fault of a patch; how the series lands is main's. Every other gate passes on each patch. 0 of 19.
